+# 11 — VS CSS: delayed preview after cursor hover
+
+**Version:** runtime-candidate research revision, 2026-09-14.
+**Inspected base:** `a5c5bc08d8e8661658865216798d600462db948e` (`master`).
+**Priority / scope:** Input-to-presentation latency.
+**Existing owner:** P2-1 compact-preview owner.
+**Status:** OPEN — candidate code/proposals, not a ROM-verified fix.
+
+Read [COMMON.md](COMMON.md). Reconcile the actual working tree, source-derived
+assets and current board before changing code. Preserve unrelated edits.
+
+## Owner report (preserved)
+
+> delay between cursor hover and 3d fighter preview rendering.
+
+## Current source findings
+
+Current CSS misses perform multiple preparation steps in one acquire action. The delay may include explicit dwell, acquisition, pose warming and deferred publication; no measured breakdown from the reported ROM was available.
+
+Source keys: [S10](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#s10), [R48](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r48), [R102](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r102).
+These distinguish directly inspected code from repository-recorded proof; none
+is a new ROM run by this package's author.
+
+## Potential runtime fix
+
+Implement separate request and resident identities with cancellation/coalescing. Serve an already-resident matching preview immediately; on a miss, reserve one available resident block and stage its data in bounded chunks. Warm only source-required idle/selected poses at an admitted loading boundary, not the entire moveset on cursor movement. Publish the newest still-requested fighter only when all resources are valid; release superseded jobs without exposing partial geometry. Reduce a dwell constant only if it is the measured remaining delay after loads are bounded.
+
+### Executable candidate diffs
+
+[R03_css_reset_image_lifetime.patch](runtime/R03_css_reset_image_lifetime.patch) — **DEFENSIVE CANDIDATE / not a complete CSS fix**.
+
+Check preimages with `python Briefs/tools/check_candidates.py --repo . --candidate R03`. Applying a patch and passing a host test do not establish natural-path correctness.
+
+Implementation contract and code-oriented integration details: [research/CSS_TRANSACTIONAL_PREVIEW.md](research/CSS_TRANSACTIONAL_PREVIEW.md).
+
+## Disprove this candidate before stacking patches
+
+Fast cursor input that repeatedly cancels jobs must not starve the final settled request, leak blocks or display the wrong fighter. Do not claim zero hover I/O simply from a warm-cache tour.
+
+## Acceptance for this symptom
+
+The correct preview appears at the source-appropriate reveal point without unexplained extra blank frames. Report input-to-visible latency distributions in frames for cold/warm sweeps, maximum delay and all-presented-frame cadence. Rapid A->B->A changes never flash the wrong fighter or stale resources.
+
+## Required regression scope
+
+BGM continuity, gate animation, all fighter previews, simultaneous panel residents, cancellation and scene exit during pending preparation.
+
+## Coordination
+
+Use the same instrumented sweep as CSS gate/music work; their acceptance remains distinct.
+
+## Closure
+
+Apply COMMON.md's natural-path, positive-engagement, source/pixel/audio, resource,
+native-only, cadence and widest-relevant-verifier requirements. Record candidate
+identity and actual coverage in the existing BUG_NOTES owner; preserve BUGS wording
+and unrelated dirty edits. Report any unrun/failed gate and owner acceptance still
+owed. No brief or host-only test closes the runtime bug. Report unverified portions explicitly.
